# Melee dodge (melee_dodge, step 6.2 of the NRFTW port): the hero with a one-hander, in front of the fixture's
# bandit in Onar's open field, dodges by its own key (`tap dodge`; the way from the movement keys held at the press)
# back, left, right and forward, and forward-left (forward wins); then by the jump key itself, the default binding
# (`tap jump`: back, with the strafe key left, with the turn key left); then back under the bandit's blow (`dodge ...
# before`: as the blow is 100 ms from its contact, so the contact comes inside the dash's window, 40-360 ms, before
# the hero is out of reach); last, in medium and heavy armour (the roll and the slow roll fall back to the dash while
# their animations are not made). After each jump-key take `anims` logs what the hero plays: `bs=27` and the dash,
# or nothing new where there is no dodge that way.
# The flag off is the same file with MELEE_DODGE=0: the `tap jump` takes jump (`anims ... bs=8 ...: S_JUMP`, or a
# climb), `tap dodge` does nothing (no `melee dodge` line), `dodge ... before` logs `refused, disabled`, and the
# blow under it hits.
# Every dodge writes `melee dodge PC_HERO: <way>, armour <class>, <move> <animation> [(no <missing names>)], cost <n>,
# window <a>-<b> ms` in bench.log, or why there is none: `no dodge this way (no ...)`, `the original jump back`,
# `refused, <reason>`. The blow inside the window writes `melee hit by BDT_1013_BANDIT_L at <ms> ms of dash 40-360 ms:
# did not pass`. OPENGOTHIC_BODY_TRACE=1 adds the `dodge*` events to body_combat. Our animations come from the content
# (scripts/content/anim/content_pack.py: T_1HDASHB for HUMANS, HUMANS_1HST1, HUMANS_1HST2 so far); the look is judged
# from the clips by the one who made them.
# WORLD=NEWWORLD.ZEN BENCH_HOST=local OPENGOTHIC_CONTENT=/abs/content
seed 73013
cheat god
set time 12 0
release all
goto NW_BIGFARM_VORPOSTEN1_01_RIGHTFIELD_02
wait 500
clear 3000
corner right go 0
melee-shadow setup 1h
wait 600
melee-shadow target 2
wait 600
pin WOLF 5000 90 0
wait 34
pin off
pin WOLF 5000 -90 0
wait 34
pin off
# The fixture's signpost stands between them at the wall: turn into the open field.
turn 180
pin BDT_1013_BANDIT_L 320 0 0
wait 300
pin off
immortal BDT_1013_BANDIT_L on
watch player
cam two BDT_1013_BANDIT_L 320 10 1
# After a goto the hero takes a move about 2 s later
wait 2000
shot start

rec dodge-back
tap dodge
wait 1200
stop

rec dodge-left
press left
tap dodge
wait 34
release left
wait 1200
stop

rec dodge-right
press right
tap dodge
wait 34
release right
wait 1200
stop

rec dodge-forward
press forward
tap dodge
wait 34
release forward
wait 1200
stop

rec dodge-forward-left
press forward
press left
tap dodge
wait 34
release all
wait 1200
stop

# The jump key is the dodge's default key while a melee weapon is drawn
rec jump-key-back
tap jump
wait 100
anims
wait 1100
stop

rec jump-key-left
press left
tap jump
wait 34
release left
wait 66
anims
wait 1100
stop

# No strafe key held: the keys that turn the hero give the side (the arrows of the preset)
rec turn-key-left
press turnl
tap jump
wait 34
release turnl
wait 66
anims
wait 1100
stop

rec under-blow
pin BDT_1013_BANDIT_L 160 0 0
wait 300
pin off
fight BDT_1013_BANDIT_L player
dodge player back before BDT_1013_BANDIT_L 100
wait 3000
stop

# Armour: medium rolls, heavy rolls slowly; until those animations exist the dash plays, at its own cost and window
freeze BDT_1013_BANDIT_L
pin BDT_1013_BANDIT_L 320 0 0
wait 300
pin off
rec dodge-medium
equip ITAR_MIL_M
wait 300
tap dodge
wait 1200
stop

rec dodge-heavy
equip ITAR_PAL_H
wait 300
tap dodge
wait 1200
stop
